# PRP — Wire tools + handlers + config + runtime in the default factory (index.ts)

## Goal

**Feature Goal**: Replace the no-op `src/index.ts` stub with the complete extension factory that wires every P1.M1–M4 module into a single loadable entry point, and ship `test/index.test.ts` proving the wiring. The factory is the package `main` + `pi.extensions["./src/index.ts"]` entry (spec/11 §1.1). After this task, `pi -e ./src/index.ts` loads cleanly with zero configuration and exposes all 4 tools + all handlers.

**Deliverable**: Two files at `/home/dustin/projects/pi-mulligan-hack`:
- `src/index.ts` — default-export factory `(pi: ExtensionAPI): void` that (a) points the logger at the cached config's `log.file`, (b) registers 4 tools, (c) attaches 5 `pi.on` handlers (session_start, context, tool_result, turn_end, session_shutdown), using ONLY imports from already-shipped sibling modules. NO new logic.
- `test/index.test.ts` — vitest suite (globals:true) asserting: factory registers exactly the 4 named tools, attaches all handlers, does not throw, loads zero-config (no settings), and `config.enabled=false` makes the context handler pass-through + every tool refuse (E14).

**Success Definition**: `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean; `npx vitest run test/index.test.ts` is green; the full `npx vitest run` suite stays green; `pi -e ./src/index.ts -p "hi"` exits 0 (zero-config load); a `grep` over `src/index.ts` confirms NO `sendUserMessage`/`registerCommand`/`registerShortcut`.

## Why

- This is the capstone wiring task of milestone M5 (spec/11 §8 Step 8). Every prior task (M1 foundation, M2 pure helpers, M3 Pi-coupled glue, M4 tools) produced independently-tested modules; NONE of them is reachable by Pi until `index.ts` registers them. Without this task the extension is a pile of unconnected modules.
- Establishes the zero-config contract (spec/09 §1, spec/11 §3 DoD #4): the extension MUST work with no `mulligan` settings block, because v1 has NO Pi-settings accessor (see Known Gotchas). `getConfig()` lazily caches validated `DEFAULT_CONFIG`; handlers read it on each fire.
- Locks in the D8/C2 constraints (spec/02): the factory MUST NOT use `pi.sendUserMessage`, `pi.registerCommand`, or `pi.registerShortcut` — a verifiable grep gate enforces this.

## What

A thin SYNC factory that delegates entirely to shipped modules. It creates no patterns of its own.

### Success Criteria
- [ ] `src/index.ts` exports `default function (pi: ExtensionAPI): void` (SYNC — no `async`, no returned Promise; spec/01 §1).
- [ ] Factory calls `setLogFile(getConfig().log.file)` exactly once at the top (points the logger; `null` default → off). `getConfig()` is called lazily by handlers elsewhere (it caches `DEFAULT_CONFIG` on first call).
- [ ] Factory registers EXACTLY 4 tools, in any order, via `pi.registerTool`: `makeRewindTool(pi)`, `makeShrinkTool(pi)`, `makeCheckpointTool(pi)` (each a FACTORY capturing `pi` via closure), and `auditTool` (a PLAIN const — audit is read-only and needs no `pi`).
- [ ] Factory attaches EXACTLY these `pi.on` handlers: `pi.on("context", contextHandler)` (inline — `filter.ts` exports the handler directly, NOT a register seam); `registerBloatReminder(pi)` (→ `pi.on("tool_result", …)`, Nudge A); `registerTurnEndMetric(pi)` (→ `pi.on("turn_end", …)`, Nudge B Phase 1); `pi.on("session_start", (_e, ctx) => resetRuntime(ctx.sessionManager.getSessionId()))`; `pi.on("session_shutdown", () => clearAll())`.
- [ ] `session_start` handler reads `ctx.sessionManager.getSessionId()` FRESH inside the callback (C12 — never cache a sessionManager handle across turns) and calls `resetRuntime(sessionId)` to drop any stale same-session runtime (the fresh runtime is created lazily by the first `runtime()` consumer; `tokenBaseline` starts `null` per `freshRuntime`).
- [ ] NO `try/catch` wraps the factory body — fail-FAST on bootstrap wiring errors (the individual handlers already self-protect for fail-open per spec/03 #4 / spec/08 E13; config loading is fail-open inside `getConfig`/`setConfig`).
- [ ] `src/index.ts` contains NO occurrence of `pi.sendUserMessage`, `pi.registerCommand`, or `pi.registerShortcut` (D8, C2 — spec/02). Also no `registerFlag`.
- [ ] `test/index.test.ts` exists and passes; full `npx vitest run` stays green (no regressions to the 594 existing tests).
- [ ] `pi -e ./src/index.ts -p "hi"` exits 0 (verified zero-config load against pi 0.84.1).

